the fire movement otherwise known as  financial independence retire early  changed our lives in ways that we had  never thought possible before  five years ago we came across dave  ramsey and we were motivated like never  before to reach financial independence  with the goal of early retirement  we sold many of our possessions  worked overtime almost every single week  cut out many of our expenses  and worked diligently to get out of debt  for the first time in our lives we  realized that we could take ownership of  our finances and build a future we  desire  one where we could be financially freed  from the rat race and actually have time  for family friends and activities that  we enjoy  one where we could give more and make a  greater impact  one in which we could be free to work on  projects and hobbies simply because we  choose to and not because we  have to make money  one where money isn't a barrier to  spending more time with our children  in many ways i am incredibly thankful  for having come across the fire movement  even much more so that my husband joined  me  it led us to minimalism and being  content with less and simplicity  it freed me from my horrible shopping  habits which i share more in detail in  my video the seven dumbest purchases i  made in my early twenties  and it fueled the fire that we needed to  build our first home a small home but a  monster of a project for two people who  had never done such a thing before  we have yet to reach our financial goals  but something has changed in me now  and that is that  i'm okay with that  you see it all sounds pretty on the  outside  we built a home and got out of debt  however we sacrificed much to get there  as a nurse i worked 12 hour shifts and  was working overtime every single week  until the point that i could no longer  manage at 9 months pregnant  once our daughter was born we sacrificed  time with her  i overworked my body trying to do more  and frustrated because i couldn't do it  fast enough  my husband injured his back and spent  sleepless nights because of uncontrolled  pain  and thousands of dollars to get  treatment  needless to say he could not work during  that time and we were unable to work on  the house  i'm incredibly thankful for the home  that we have because it was built  through literal blood sweat and tears  and it was not without sacrifice  i am now a mom of two young children i  still have a full-time job but my  perspective has changed  greatly  i now long to savor simple moments  to explore the beauty of slow  intentional living  to allow myself to spend money on myself  every now and then without feeling guilt  to give myself permission to say no to  the constant text messages requesting  for me to work overtime and most  importantly to enjoy each day as though  it were my last  my patience changed my perspective on  life  you see  i now work as a hospice nurse  every day that i work i am faced with  the concept of death and dying  i assist patients who are at the end of  life to better manage their symptoms so  that they can live their life to their  fullest for however long that might be  and through these individuals i have  learned that it is not the big  accomplishments and hurdles that we  cross that truly bring us joy in the  long run  for my patients  it is the simplest of moments that bring  tears of joy to their eyes  it's being able to be at home with their  puppy on their lap it's being able to  see their grandchildren laugh and play  it's controlling the nausea just enough  to enjoy their loved morning coffee  it's seeing a bird outside the window  it's being surrounded by the people they  love most  looking back i realized that i became so  obsessed with doing more achieving more  and doing it all faster that i  sacrificed the thing that i most  treasure  in order to accomplish a goal at some  point in the future  a time  that may never happen  i still hold value to the categories  give save spend and invest but i now  realize that there is so much more to it  than that  that life is precious  that every day i am able to work my  patients deserve my complete presence  and attention  that i ought to work on the things that  i enjoy and have time for myself  that every day with my family is a gift  that every day i walk and breathe  i am blessed in some way  i hope this video encourages you to not  only place a focus on creating financial  goals and seek a specific target a  specific destination  but to enjoy the ride  to enjoy the process of getting there  when hiking to the top of the mountain  the view is incredible but don't just  enjoy the view at the top  be sure to enjoy the sights on the way  up  and this is why i quit the fire movement  in favor of slow and intentional living  if you enjoyed this video please give it  a thumbs up and share with your friends  and don't forget to subscribe so you  won't miss when i post a new video  i thank you so much for watching until  next time
 

